      "message": "From a user\u0027s perspective, there shouldn\u0027t be much difference at the moment other than (hopefully) somewhat faster build times due to caching + use of Swarming for running tests. There are a number of other benefits behind the scenes that Yuly pointed out, though. The `-sws-` bots are meant to provide the same compile/test coverage as the existing Dawn standalone builders that do everything directly in the recipe.\n\nLonger-term, we\u0027ll also be able to run Dawn standalone tests on real hardware instead of relying on the Chromium builders.",
